-- 046: Deep content + matching exercises for X10 · Advanced Data Analysis (RFM). Upscale.
UPDATE public.sessions SET
 content_en = E'> 🚀 **Upscale** session — available to Extended-track learners.\n\n## Why not all customers are equal\n\nTreating every customer the same wastes budget. **Segmentation** groups customers by behaviour so you can act differently on each group. **RFM** is the classic, no-machine-learning-needed way to do it — and it maps directly to money.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Segmentation & clustering\n\n**Segmentation** splits customers into meaningful groups. You can do it by rules (RFM) or by algorithms (k-means clustering). Use it for **retention** (who is slipping away?) and **targeting** (who deserves the premium offer?).\n\n---\n\n## 2. The RFM model\n\nThree behavioural signals, all computable from an orders table:\n\n| Dimension | Question | From the data |\n|-----------|----------|---------------|\n| **Recency** | How recently did they buy? | days since last order (lower = better) |\n| **Frequency** | How often do they buy? | count of orders |\n| **Monetary** | How much do they spend? | sum of order value |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Scoring RFM\n\nRank customers into 1–5 on each dimension (5 = best). A common method: split each dimension into quintiles.\n\n| Customer | Days since last | Orders | Total spend | R | F | M | RFM |\n|----------|-----------------|--------|-------------|---|---|---|-----|\n| Budi | 5 | 12 | 30,000,000 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 555 |\n| Siti | 90 | 3 | 2,000,000 | 2 | 3 | 2 | 232 |\n| Ahmad | 300 | 1 | 300,000 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 111 |\n\n> Recency is scored **inverted** — fewer days since the last order earns a *higher* R.\n\n---\n\n## 4. From scores to segments\n\n| Segment | RFM pattern | Meaning |\n|---------|-------------|---------|\n| **Champions** | high R, high F, high M | best customers, recent & valuable |\n| **Loyal** | high F, decent M | buy often, keep them happy |\n| **At Risk** | low R, once-high F/M | used to be great, going quiet |\n| **New** | high R, low F | just arrived, nurture them |\n| **Lost** | low R, low F, low M | long inactive |\n\n---\n\n## 5. From segments to action\n\n| Segment | Recommended action |\n|---------|--------------------|\n| Champions | Reward, upsell premium, ask for referrals |\n| At Risk | Win-back offer before they churn |\n| New | Onboarding nurture, second-purchase nudge |\n| Lost | One reactivation attempt, then stop spending on them |\n\n> **Mini case study.** TokoSegar scored 15,000 customers. The 8% "At Risk" segment held 24% of last year''s revenue. A targeted win-back email to just that group recovered more than a blanket discount to everyone — at a fraction of the cost.\n\n---\n\n## Common pitfalls\n\n- **Scoring recency the wrong way** — more days = *lower* R, not higher.\n- **Equal-width instead of quintile bins** — a few whales distort raw monetary ranges; rank into quintiles.\n- **Too many micro-segments** — 125 RFM cells are unusable; roll them into ~5 named segments.\n- **Segmenting with no action** — a segment nobody acts on is just a label.\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| Segmentation | Grouping customers by behaviour |\n| RFM | Recency, Frequency, Monetary scoring |\n| Quintile | A 1-in-5 rank bucket |\n| Champions | Recent, frequent, high-spend customers |\n| At Risk | Previously valuable customers going quiet |\n\n---\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n1. Segmentation lets you treat different customers differently — for retention and targeting.\n2. **RFM** = **Recency** (how recent), **Frequency** (how often), **Monetary** (how much).\n3. Score each dimension **1–5** (quintiles); recency is inverted.\n4. Roll scores into a handful of named **segments** (Champions, At Risk, New, Lost…).\n5. Every segment must map to an **action** — otherwise it is just a label.\n\n> 💡 Practice with the matching exercises below, then run an RFM segmentation on the assignment dataset.',
 content_id = E'> 🚀 Sesi **Upscale** — tersedia untuk peserta jalur Extended.\n\n## Kenapa tidak semua pelanggan sama\n\nMemperlakukan setiap pelanggan sama membuang anggaran. **Segmentasi** mengelompokkan pelanggan berdasarkan perilaku agar Anda bisa bertindak berbeda pada tiap grup. **RFM** adalah cara klasik tanpa perlu machine learning — dan ia langsung terkait ke uang.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Segmentasi & clustering\n\n**Segmentasi** membagi pelanggan menjadi grup bermakna. Bisa lewat aturan (RFM) atau algoritma (k-means clustering). Gunakan untuk **retensi** (siapa yang menjauh?) dan **targeting** (siapa yang layak penawaran premium?).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Model RFM\n\nTiga sinyal perilaku, semua bisa dihitung dari tabel orders:\n\n| Dimensi | Pertanyaan | Dari data |\n|---------|------------|-----------|\n| **Recency** | Seberapa baru mereka beli? | hari sejak order terakhir (makin kecil makin baik) |\n| **Frequency** | Seberapa sering mereka beli? | jumlah order |\n| **Monetary** | Seberapa banyak mereka belanja? | total nilai order |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Menghitung skor RFM\n\nBeri peringkat pelanggan 1–5 di tiap dimensi (5 = terbaik). Metode umum: bagi tiap dimensi menjadi kuintil.\n\n| Pelanggan | Hari sejak terakhir | Order | Total belanja | R | F | M | RFM |\n|-----------|---------------------|-------|---------------|---|---|---|-----|\n| Budi | 5 | 12 | 30.000.000 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 555 |\n| Siti | 90 | 3 | 2.000.000 | 2 | 3 | 2 | 232 |\n| Ahmad | 300 | 1 | 300.000 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 111 |\n\n> Recency diberi skor **terbalik** — makin sedikit hari sejak order terakhir, makin *tinggi* R.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Dari skor ke segmen\n\n| Segmen | Pola RFM | Makna |\n|--------|----------|-------|\n| **Champions** | R tinggi, F tinggi, M tinggi | pelanggan terbaik, baru & bernilai |\n| **Loyal** | F tinggi, M layak | sering beli, jaga kepuasan mereka |\n| **At Risk** | R rendah, dulu F/M tinggi | dulu hebat, mulai sepi |\n| **New** | R tinggi, F rendah | baru datang, dirawat |\n| **Lost** | R rendah, F rendah, M rendah | lama tidak aktif |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Dari segmen ke aksi\n\n| Segmen | Aksi yang disarankan |\n|--------|----------------------|\n| Champions | Beri reward, upsell premium, minta referral |\n| At Risk | Penawaran win-back sebelum churn |\n| New | Nurture onboarding, dorong pembelian kedua |\n| Lost | Satu upaya reaktivasi, lalu berhenti membelanjakan untuk mereka |\n\n> **Studi kasus mini.** TokoSegar menskor 15.000 pelanggan. Segmen "At Risk" yang 8% memegang 24% revenue tahun lalu. Email win-back tertarget hanya ke grup itu memulihkan lebih banyak dibanding diskon merata ke semua — dengan biaya jauh lebih kecil.\n\n---\n\n## Kesalahan umum\n\n- **Menskor recency terbalik** — lebih banyak hari = R *lebih rendah*, bukan lebih tinggi.\n- **Bin lebar-sama alih-alih kuintil** — beberapa whale mendistorsi rentang monetary mentah; ranking ke kuintil.\n- **Terlalu banyak mikro-segmen** — 125 sel RFM tak terpakai; gulung jadi ~5 segmen bernama.\n- **Segmentasi tanpa aksi** — segmen yang tak ditindaklanjuti hanya label.\n\n---\n\n## Glosarium\n\n| Istilah | Arti |\n|---------|------|\n| Segmentasi | Mengelompokkan pelanggan berdasarkan perilaku |\n| RFM | Skoring Recency, Frequency, Monetary |\n| Kuintil | Bucket peringkat 1-dari-5 |\n| Champions | Pelanggan baru, sering, belanja tinggi |\n| At Risk | Pelanggan yang dulu bernilai, mulai sepi |\n\n---\n\n## Kesimpulan Utama\n\n1. Segmentasi memungkinkan memperlakukan pelanggan berbeda secara berbeda — untuk retensi dan targeting.\n2. **RFM** = **Recency** (seberapa baru), **Frequency** (seberapa sering), **Monetary** (seberapa banyak).\n3. Skor tiap dimensi **1–5** (kuintil); recency terbalik.\n4. Gulung skor menjadi beberapa **segmen** bernama (Champions, At Risk, New, Lost…).\n5. Setiap segmen harus terpetakan ke **aksi** — kalau tidak, hanya label.\n\n> 💡 Latih dengan exercise matching di bawah, lalu jalankan segmentasi RFM pada dataset tugas.'
WHERE session_number = 'X10';

INSERT INTO public.exercises (session_id, type, title_en, title_id, description_en, description_id, starter_code, solution_code, test_cases, hints_en, hints_id, difficulty, order_num)
SELECT s.id, 'matching', 'RFM Letters', 'Huruf RFM',
  'Match each RFM letter to what it measures.', 'Cocokkan setiap huruf RFM dengan yang diukurnya.',
  '{"pairs":[{"left":"Recency","right":"How recently they bought"},{"left":"Frequency","right":"How often they buy"},{"left":"Monetary","right":"How much they spend"},{"left":"RFM score","right":"Combines all three signals"}]}','',
  '[{"id":"tc1","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"How recently they bought","description_en":"R","description_id":"R","points":25},{"id":"tc2","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"How often they buy","description_en":"F","description_id":"F","points":25},{"id":"tc3","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"How much they spend","description_en":"M","description_id":"M","points":25},{"id":"tc4","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Combines all three signals","description_en":"RFM","description_id":"RFM","points":25}]',
  '["R is about time since last order","M is about money"]','["R soal waktu sejak order terakhir","M soal uang"]','easy',1
FROM public.sessions s WHERE s.session_number='X10' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.exercises e WHERE e.session_id=s.id AND e.title_en='RFM Letters');

INSERT INTO public.exercises (session_id, type, title_en, title_id, description_en, description_id, starter_code, solution_code, test_cases, hints_en, hints_id, difficulty, order_num)
SELECT s.id, 'matching', 'RFM Segments', 'Segmen RFM',
  'Match each segment to its description.', 'Cocokkan setiap segmen dengan deskripsinya.',
  '{"pairs":[{"left":"Champions","right":"Recent, frequent, high spend"},{"left":"At Risk","right":"Used to buy, now going quiet"},{"left":"New","right":"Just made a first purchase"},{"left":"Lost","right":"Long inactive"}]}','',
  '[{"id":"tc1","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Recent, frequent, high spend","description_en":"Champions","description_id":"Champions","points":25},{"id":"tc2","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Used to buy, now going quiet","description_en":"At Risk","description_id":"At Risk","points":25},{"id":"tc3","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Just made a first purchase","description_en":"New","description_id":"New","points":25},{"id":"tc4","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Long inactive","description_en":"Lost","description_id":"Lost","points":25}]',
  '["Champions score high everywhere","Lost have not bought in ages"]','["Champions skor tinggi di semua","Lost sudah lama tak beli"]','easy',2
FROM public.sessions s WHERE s.session_number='X10' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.exercises e WHERE e.session_id=s.id AND e.title_en='RFM Segments');

INSERT INTO public.exercises (session_id, type, title_en, title_id, description_en, description_id, starter_code, solution_code, test_cases, hints_en, hints_id, difficulty, order_num)
SELECT s.id, 'matching', 'Customer to RFM Score', 'Pelanggan ke Skor RFM',
  'Match each customer to their RFM score pattern.', 'Cocokkan setiap pelanggan dengan pola skor RFM-nya.',
  '{"pairs":[{"left":"Bought yesterday, often, big spender","right":"555"},{"left":"Bought long ago, once, tiny spend","right":"111"},{"left":"Bought yesterday but only once","right":"High R, low F"},{"left":"Frequent and big, but not recently","right":"Low R, high F and M"}]}','',
  '[{"id":"tc1","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"555","description_en":"Champion","description_id":"Champion","points":25},{"id":"tc2","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"111","description_en":"Lost","description_id":"Lost","points":25},{"id":"tc3","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"High R, low F","description_en":"New","description_id":"New","points":25},{"id":"tc4","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Low R, high F and M","description_en":"At Risk","description_id":"At Risk","points":25}]',
  '["Recent = high R","Not recently = low R even if F/M high"]','["Baru = R tinggi","Tidak baru = R rendah walau F/M tinggi"]','medium',3
FROM public.sessions s WHERE s.session_number='X10' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.exercises e WHERE e.session_id=s.id AND e.title_en='Customer to RFM Score');

INSERT INTO public.exercises (session_id, type, title_en, title_id, description_en, description_id, starter_code, solution_code, test_cases, hints_en, hints_id, difficulty, order_num)
